# Pitchframe environment template.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in what you have. `.env` is gitignored, and it
# should stay that way — an endpoint URL is a subscription identifier.
#
# Nothing here is required. With an empty `.env` the system selects the offline
# tier and runs end to end on scripted replies, which is how the repository stays
# testable by someone who does not have an Azure subscription.

# --- Tier 1: Azure AI Foundry (the intended production path) -----------------
#
# The endpoint of your Foundry *project*, not the account. Find it in the Azure AI
# Foundry portal under the project's overview.
#
# No API key belongs here. Authentication goes through AzureCliCredential, so the
# only prerequisite on a fresh machine is `az login`. A credential object cannot be
# pasted into a chat window, committed by accident, or scraped from a log.
AZURE_AI_PROJECT_ENDPOINT=

# The name you gave the model deployment, which is not always the model's own name.
AZURE_AI_MODEL_DEPLOYMENT=

# --- Tier 3: Ollama (local server, no Azure) --------------------------------
#
# Set this to use a local model when Foundry is unreachable or unconfigured.
# Leave it empty to skip the tier entirely.
OLLAMA_HOST=

# --- Behaviour --------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Force a tier instead of auto-selecting, strongest first. Useful for recording a
# reproducible demo, or for proving the parser works with a small local model.
# One of: foundry, local, ollama, offline
PITCHFRAME_PROVIDER=
